{"name":"Fern Canopy","hex":"#758a5f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of some twenty thousand species of vascular plants classified in the division Pteridophyta that lack seeds and reproduce by shedding spores to initiate an alternation of generations.","A light green color inspired by the color of ferns."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fern"},{"term":"canopy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A high cover providing shelter, such as a cloth supported above an object, particularly over a bed.","Any overhanging or projecting roof structure, typically over entrances or doors."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with or as if with a canopy.","To go through the canopy of a forest on a zipline."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canopy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fern","blocks":[{"text":"Ferns are a group of vascular plants that reproduce via spores and have neither seeds nor flowers. They reproduce in two phases, a short-lived gametophyte that reproduces sexually to develop a spore-bearing leaf structure. Some ferns produce coiled fiddleheads, which expand into fronds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg/330px-The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fern"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Equisetopsida.jpg/500px-Equisetopsida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Equisetopsida.jpg/500px-Equisetopsida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut